    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the fan cowl latch assembly, its keeper, the aperture seal and the clamp set, showing the flagged and the original latch standards and the placard that prohibits mixing them.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "To identify the fan cowl latch assembly, its keeper, the aperture seal and the associated clamps and shrouds on both nacelles.",
      "figure_note": "The figure is drawn looking inboard at the left-hand fan cowl with the cowl open; the right-hand installation is a mirror image. Item 10 and item 10A are the shroud kit at the flagged and the original latch standards, and they are not interchangeable because the keeper aperture differs. Two latches are fitted per cowl and both must be to the same standard: the placard at item 80 is applied when the flagged standard is fitted and states the prohibition. The seal at item 30 is discarded at every removal and must be ordered with any latch work."
    },
